From 2b7ec3abf52cbb469e768760601f7af1be43feee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Govindaraj Saminathan <govindaraj.saminathan@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 16:30:41 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: Reset num_multi_hws on interface cleanup

hostapd_cleanup_iface_partial() frees and NULLs iface->multi_hw_info but
leaves iface->num_multi_hws at its previous non-zero value.  If
hostapd_set_current_hw_info() is called after a partial cleanup (e.g.,
during interface restart), it skips the early return and dereferences
the already-freed multi_hw_info array.

Reset num_multi_hws to 0 alongside the NULL assignment so the two fields
remain consistent.

Signed-off-by: Govindaraj Saminathan <govindaraj.saminathan@oss.qualcomm.com>
---
 src/ap/hostapd.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/ap/hostapd.c b/src/ap/hostapd.c
index fb60462..b5f713f 100644
--- a/src/ap/hostapd.c
+++ b/src/ap/hostapd.c
@@ -742,6 +742,7 @@ void hostapd_cleanup_iface_partial(struct hostapd_iface *iface)
 	airtime_policy_update_deinit(iface);
 	hostapd_free_multi_hw_info(iface->multi_hw_info);
 	iface->multi_hw_info = NULL;
+	iface->num_multi_hws = 0;
 	iface->current_hw_info = NULL;
 }
 
